.Dd August 23, 2026
.Dt AUTODO.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm autodo.conf
.Nd configuration file for the autodo-eventd daemon
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the
.Xr autodo-eventd 8
configuration file, in UCL format
.Pa ( /usr/local/etc/autodo/autodo.conf
by default).
It controls which groups receive implicit privileges from the
.Xr mac_do_auto 4
kernel module, the scope of those privileges, the path deny list, and
audit logging.
.Pp
The daemon reloads the file automatically on change or on
.Dv SIGHUP .
.Sh DIRECTIVES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va enabled = true | false
Master switch (default: true).
When false, a zero-permission policy is pushed and the path deny list
is cleared.
.It Va profile_dir = Ar path
Directory containing named policy profiles
(default:
.Pa /usr/local/etc/autodo/profiles ) .
.El
.Sh GROUPS
The
.Va groups
block maps group names (resolved with
.Xr getgrnam 3 )
to policy.
Each entry either references a named profile or defines an inline
scope:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
groups {
    wheel {
        profile = "all";
    }
    operators {
        scope {
            categories = ["vfs", "net"];
        }
        deny {
            privileges = ["PRIV_VFS_MOUNT"];
        }
    }
}
.Ed
.Pp
Categories correspond to families of
.Xr priv 9
constants:
.Li system , audit , cred , debug , jail , kld , proc , vfs , vm , dev ,
.Li net ,
.Li misc ,
or
.Li all .
The
.Va deny privileges
list removes individual privileges from the compiled scope.
.Pp
When the
.Va groups
block is absent, the legacy single-group behavior applies: the group in
.Va security.mac.autodo.gid
receives the scope from the top-level
.Va scope
directive.
.Sh PATH DENY LIST
The top-level
.Va deny paths
list names absolute path prefixes that autodo-elevated users may not
modify:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
deny {
    paths = ["/boot/kernel", "/bin", "/sbin"];
}
.Ed
.Pp
Create, delete, rename, mkdir, write, chmod/chown, and flag changes
under these prefixes are denied for non-root members of managed groups,
even when the module would otherwise grant the privilege.
Root is exempt; reads are unaffected.
See
.Xr mac_do_auto 4
for the exact semantics and limitations.
.Sh AUDIT
The
.Va audit
block controls event logging:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
audit {
    enabled = true;
    log_file = "/var/log/autodo/events.json";
}
.Ed
.Pp
Events are appended as JSON lines with fields
.Va ts , pid , uid , gid , priv , granted ,
and
.Va comm .
.Sh PROFILES
A profile is a UCL file in
.Va profile_dir
with the same
.Va scope
and
.Va deny
structure as an inline group entry, plus an optional
.Va description :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
description = "Minimal: file system access only";
scope {
    categories = ["vfs"];
}
.Ed
.Pp
Stock profiles:
.Li all
(everything),
.Li minimal
(vfs only),
.Li developer ,
and
.Li server-admin .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/autodo/autodo.conf
Configuration file.
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/autodo/profiles/
Policy profile directory.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mac_do_auto 4 ,
.Xr autodo-eventd 8
